A '''Madame''' (Japanese: '''マダム''' ''Madame''), known as a '''Socialite''' until [[Generation VI]], is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] introduced in [[Generation IV]]. They are depicted as rich, older women wearing exquisite clothing and accessories. Madames will generally use [[Pokémon]] based on pets or other "refined" Pokémon, like {{p|Roselia}}.

In the [[Battle Subway]] in [[Generation V]], Socialites specialize in [[Legendary Pokémon]] during later battles.

In [[Generation VI]], this {{DL|Pokémon Trainer|Trainer class}} only appears in the [[Battle Maison]], but Madames can also be found in {{g|X and Y}} at the [[Battle Chateau]] as a {{tc|Baroness}}, {{tc|Viscountess}}, {{tc|Countess}}, {{tc|Marchioness}}, or {{tc|Duchess}}. Their male counterparts appear to be the {{tc|Gentleman}} and {{tc|Monsieur}} classes.

In Generations {{gen|VII}} and {{gen|VIII}}, they keep their Pokémon in [[Luxury Ball]]s. In the [[Battle Tree]], Madames who appear after the {{tc|Battle Legend}} will primarily use Legendary Pokémon.

